Migration commands for this branch:

    flask --app app db upgrade head
    flask --app app db downgrade base

Review the target DATABASE_URL before running either command. Upgrade head
preserves the legacy JSON column while copying its content into relational
tables and adds a gradebook concurrency version. Downgrade base removes the
relational tables and added version column while leaving the legacy JSON in
place; application writes keep it synchronized during the compatibility window.

On a disposable copy of the target database, run the read-only JSON preflight
before the migration:

    flask --app app preflight-gradebooks

After upgrade, compare both representations and their averages with:

    flask --app app audit-gradebooks

These commands report profile and grade counts and averages, exit with status 1
if they find invalid or inconsistent data, and never repair or modify data.

The initial migration validates every legacy profile before changing the
schema. If a profile is invalid, it reports the profile ID and stops before
creating relational tables or adding compatibility columns.
